Implemented the PRD in [page.tsx](/Users/moltbot/pp-agent-work/factory-idea-054/src/app/pp/deploy-requests/[requestId]/page.tsx) and [review-page-helpers.tsx](/Users/moltbot/pp-agent-work/factory-idea-054/src/app/pp/deploy-requests/[requestId]/review-page-helpers.tsx), with focused coverage in [review-page-helpers.test.ts](/Users/moltbot/pp-agent-work/factory-idea-054/tests/review-page-helpers.test.ts).

The UI behavior now matches the acceptance criteria:
- “Setting up checks...” only shows with a spinner when merge readiness is still loading and `checks_total === 0`.
- If all checks are passing, the spinner is suppressed even when `mergeable_state === 'unknown'`.
- In that `unknown + checks passing` case, the page shows `Waiting for GitHub to confirm mergeability...` as subtle non-spinner text.

Verification: `npx vitest run tests/review-page-helpers.test.ts` passed.

I could not create the requested git commit because the sandbox blocks writes inside `.git` and `git add` failed with `Unable to create '.git/index.lock': Operation not permitted`. The commit you can run locally is:

```bash
git add 'src/app/pp/deploy-requests/[requestId]/page.tsx' \
        'src/app/pp/deploy-requests/[requestId]/review-page-helpers.tsx' \
        tests/review-page-helpers.test.ts
git commit -m "Fix merge readiness checks spinner race"
```
